  "source_rule_revision": "V1.9.0 adds static-world/dynamic-actor/camera state separation, stable IDs and project state as source of truth, project-specific timebase/integer frames, human keyframe locks, read-edit-validate-local-undo workflow, multi-view character anchors for large-angle camera motion, and reference-image responsibility mapping. V2.10.6 adds explicit per-shot facial performance states and cross-generation-segment entry/progression/exit inheritance, preventing unsupported neutral-face resets while preserving intentional restrained/poker-face acting; adds an independent zombie-face QA gate. SCG V1.1 adds machine-readable generation_segments with verified model-duration evidence and per-person facial_performance state transitions; the V1.1 validator checks segment ownership/time continuity, facial-state completeness, inherit/change semantics, offscreen carry-forward and event references. Added 21 positive/negative fixtures, extracted-ZIP SHA-256 validation and CI artifact packaging. Textual source rules remain V2.10.6; this is a supplemental structured SCG contract."
